  ==============================================
   KickOS 0.5.1  -  microkernel RTOS
  ==============================================
   board   rx72m
   arch    rxv3
   cpu     rxv3
   mpu     enforce
   sched   tickless

[reclaimwit] console reclaim + terminate drain witness
[reclaimwit] HOW TO READ THIS CAPTURE:
[reclaimwit]  1. this block is on the wire, so the kernel owns the console
[reclaimwit]  2. the app now publishes the console to a driver it spawns
[reclaimwit]  3. that driver never writes to a console, so the wire must go
[reclaimwit]     silent: a MUTE line below must occur ZERO times
[reclaimwit]  4. the app then SLAYS the driver and prints a LIVE line with
[reclaimwit]     the same kos_print call the MUTE line used
[reclaimwit]  5. LIVE present + MUTE absent == arch_console_reclaim fired.
[reclaimwit]     MUTE present == the publish never took, verdict void.
[reclaimwit]     both absent == the reclaim did not fire, console still dark.
[reclaimwit] LIVE kernel console after the driver died
[reclaimwit]   handle_close rc=0
[reclaimwit]   driver serve bytes rc=58
[reclaimwit]   slay rc=0
[reclaimwit]   post-death send (want -KOS_ECONNREFUSED) rc=-111
[reclaimwit] PASS reclaim fired: driver slain, endpoint refused, wire back
[reclaimwit] drain arm: kickos_terminate follows. The ring is disarmed in
[reclaimwit] RECLAIMED, so arch_console_flush_sync alone holds the core until
[reclaimwit] the shift register empties. The capture must END with the next
[reclaimwit] line INTACT, sentinel included; a short tail is a drain that
[reclaimwit] did not complete before arch_shutdown stopped the core.
[reclaimwit] DRAINTAIL 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef <<<DRAIN-END>>>
